--- body ---
## Context

`scripts/figures/export_corpus_table.py::_write_md_table` builds each row by
`" | ".join(vals)` where `vals` carries `str(v)` straight from the summary
DataFrame. That is exactly the shape ticket 0325 fixed in the codebook and 0339
fixed in both venue tables: a value carrying a `|` ends its cell, and the
renderer drops the overflow instead of erroring.

The standing guard from ticket 0340 cannot catch this one today. Its target,
`deliverables/_shared/tables/tab_corpus_sources.md`, is not git-tracked and is
absent on a checkout without corpus data, so the sweep skips it. The defect is
therefore live and invisible: it will surface the first time a source label or
a formatted statistic contains a pipe, on a machine that has the corpus.

Whether a *current* source label contains a pipe is not the question the fix
turns on — the point of the escaper is that no emitter has to know.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/figures/export_corpus_table.py:89-107` — `_write_md_table`, the
  unescaped interpolation
- `scripts/_markdown_table.py` — `markdown_text_cell`, the escaper for plain
  text with no markup intent
- `tests/test_corpus_table_export.py` — where the regression test belongs
- `tests/test_markdown_table_shape.py` — the 0340 sweep that will cover the
  artifact once it is built

## Actions

1. Route every interpolated value in `_write_md_table` through
   `markdown_text_cell`. Note the `**{v}**` TOTAL-row branch: escape the value,
   then wrap in the emphasis markers, not the reverse.
2. Check the caption constant on the same path.
3. Sweep the other `export_*` emitters for the same shape — this ticket was
   found by reading one of them, so the read should be finished. **Done** (PR
   #1172 round-2 gate); the sweep found three more, so the fix is four files,
   not one:

   | emitter | artifact | shape |
   |:--|:--|:--|
   | `export_corpus_table.py` | `tab_corpus_sources.md` | `str(v)` for every column |
   | `export_language_table.py` | `tab_languages.md` | `str(v)` for every column *and* the header row |
   | `export_citation_coverage.py` | `tab_citation_coverage.md` | raw `{label}` |
   | `export_corpus_flow.py` | `tab_corpus_flow.md` | raw `{row['Stage']}` |

   `export_corpus_flow.py` arrived from main (ticket 0327) after this ticket was
   filed, which is the argument for the generic exit criterion below rather than
   a per-file one. The other five emitters are clean: `export_tab_venues.py`,
   `export_core_venues_markdown.py`, `export_retrieval_protocol.py` and
   `_deposit_variables.py` route every free-text column through
   `markdown_text_cell` / `markdown_cell`, and `export_variables_table.py` and
   `export_codebook.py` interpolate nothing.

## Test

Red first, in `tests/test_corpus_table_export.py`: feed `_write_md_table` a
summary whose `Source` carries a literal `|`, render the result through
`tests/_gfm_render.py`, and assert the row keeps its eight declared cells and
the value survives intact. Assert on the *rendered* row, not on the escape —
0325 established that asserting on the escape only restates the fix.

## Verification

- [ ] The rendered row keeps eight cells with a piped source label
- [ ] The TOTAL row is still bold, and its value still escaped
- [ ] Regenerating `tab_corpus_sources.md` on a corpus machine is a no-op for
      every value that contains no escapable character
- [ ] `make lint` and `make check-fast` hold

## Invariants

- No change to the shipped table for values that need no escaping — a
  regeneration that churns every row is a failed fix.
- The `.csv` sibling output is unaffected: escaping is a Markdown concern.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No emitter in `scripts/figures/` interpolates unescaped free text into a
      pipe table
